  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "As of March 17, 2026, Susie Wiles is the White House Chief of Staff, serving in the administration of President Donald Trump since January 20, 2025. She is a veteran Republican strategist who previously managed Trump’s 2024 campaign. Wiles announced on March 16, 2026, that she is undergoing treatment for early-stage breast cancer but plans to continue her duties. Key Information regarding Susie Wiles: Role: First female White House Chief of Staff. Background: Managed Trump's 2024 presidential campaign, worked as a top aide in his Save America PAC, and advised Florida Governor Ron DeSantis. Health: On March 16, 2026, she disclosed a diagnosis of early-stage breast cancer, stating she will continue to serve while undergoing treatment with a strong prognosis. Support: President Trump publicly supported Wiles, calling her an \"amazing fighter\" and stating she will continue her work. The White House Chief of Staff is the highest-ranking employee in the White House Office, managing the president's schedule, staff, and information flow.",
